  'research-methods-in-criminal-justice',
  null,
  'Research Methods in Criminal Justice',
  'Research Methods in Criminal Justice',
  'Frame criminal justice research as systematic inquiry into crime, victimization, policing, courts, corrections, communities, and public policy. Students turn justice problems into researchable questions grounded in theory and prior evidence, protect people, communities, records, and institutions, and learn how design, measurement, and sampling shape credible claims. Topics cover surveys and victimization research, qualitative interviews and ethnography, field observation and agency research, experiments and program evaluation, official records, descriptive and inferential statistics, regression and introductory causal inference, mixed methods, reproducible workflows, equity and responsible analytics, and research reporting.',
  $rmcjjson${"slug": "research-methods-in-criminal-justice", "title": "Research Methods in Criminal Justice", "description": "Frame criminal justice research as systematic inquiry into crime, victimization, policing, courts, corrections, communities, and public policy. Students turn justice problems into researchable questions grounded in theory and prior evidence, protect people, communities, records, and institutions, and learn how design, measurement, and sampling shape credible claims. Topics cover surveys and victimization research, qualitative interviews and ethnography, field observation and agency research, experiments and program evaluation, official records, descriptive and inferential statistics, regression and introductory causal inference, mixed methods, reproducible workflows, equity and responsible analytics, and research reporting.", "topics": [{"id": "6f633abe-04fa-449f-b45d-759fae5a8b28", "type": "topic", "title": "Criminal Justice Research, Scientific Inquiry, and Evidence", "description": "Frame criminal justice research as systematic inquiry into crime, victimization, policing, courts, corrections, communities, and public policy.", "children": [{"id": "fe5af87d-47e2-4115-a974-b783717ce156", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scientific method in criminal justice", "children": [{"id": "64898c85-bb64-46a0-bbb0-35f7cd9d5b83", "type": "concept", "title": "Observation"}, {"id": "ca3d35c7-bce4-4016-b840-7de08b038070", "type": "concept", "title": "Theory"}, {"id": "b6ec9977-e7be-40f8-ae61-9f054080701c", "type": "concept", "title": "Hypothesis"}, {"id": "9f63d1de-242a-4b94-ba27-12d6211ab0e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence and revision"}], "description": "The scientific method makes justice claims testable, transparent, and open to revision."}, {"id": "d7137885-3ce6-48c1-8976-c001cc8f6e9d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "What criminal justice researchers study", "children": [{"id": "fe6ebb4d-a7d0-489c-9e7c-068135cdb8a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Crime and victimization"}, {"id": "7c3fb1d2-fe08-423d-8a04-89dda937b046", "type": "concept", "title": "Police behavior"}, {"id": "42ffffdb-d9c9-48f4-8577-4ae6be3f5cdb", "type": "concept", "title": "Court processing"}, {"id": "dcc36ac6-65b0-410d-b0d5-312d80e290f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Corrections and reentry"}], "description": "Students see research as a way to understand institutions, decisions, harms, and outcomes."}, {"id": "a59d1b35-9eb0-4d27-ae7e-dc63d8df6d9a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence standards", "children": [{"id": "49e18571-2840-4ed4-a84b-a3ffeef6736c", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive evidence"}, {"id": "70c54fb9-21b7-4dd0-b101-73c29503aa8d", "type": "concept", "title": "Causal evidence"}, {"id": "8c046bf0-20cc-45d3-9119-1b7519b0bf44", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation evidence"}, {"id": "f021c1e6-9769-4633-a82e-99c873629028", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy relevance"}], "description": "Different questions require different kinds of evidence and different levels of certainty."}]}, {"id": "8bd9700b-918c-4722-9de6-40fa6ec6d347", "type": "topic", "title": "Research Questions, Theory, and Literature Reviews", "description": "Turn justice problems into researchable questions grounded in theory and prior evidence.", "children": [{"id": "6530cb05-f249-4cc5-a31d-fb69d9bdde31", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Researchable questions", "children": [{"id": "2c4a8f69-c927-4abd-b8a9-a3ce96449cdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive questions"}, {"id": "5b548d72-dd22-4f67-b679-877d81d643ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Causal questions"}, {"id": "c5d57a19-7b82-4876-99ab-411b5a7f2f70", "type": "concept", "title": "Evaluation questions"}, {"id": "67c3821d-fe5e-4073-ae16-d463a6144e7b", "type": "concept", "title": "Normative vs empirical questions"}], "description": "A strong question is specific, answerable, important, and connected to evidence."}, {"id": "bcf701ae-21f3-41ad-861c-177a075250a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Theory and conceptual framing", "children": [{"id": "50cc9ee9-2f09-4402-9516-4afea565f306", "type": "concept", "title": "Criminological theory"}, {"id": "c0b3b592-e282-4fcd-8fe5-887353d7ef61", "type": "concept", "title": "Organizational theory"}, {"id": "efeb61fa-6e1b-4d50-8196-be6163aad6d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Procedural justice"}, {"id": "45b56c44-23e9-4c9a-9b72-1f50e1f3ac18", "type": "concept", "title": "Deterrence and opportunity"}], "description": "Theory explains why a justice outcome might occur and what mechanisms link causes to effects."}, {"id": "00643cf7-2bd0-447a-be60-4ec14a2904e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Literature review", "children": [{"id": "3103a67d-47df-4a3a-9b35-81266c806d38", "type": "concept", "title": "Search strategies"}, {"id": "a8de72d4-7c4a-4daf-9cd6-5b431d51cb3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Source quality"}, {"id": "6915e36f-2204-44d2-b40b-edffb9e6d6e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Synthesis"}, {"id": "8b39f1be-2083-48b5-9d71-208ab012bf70", "type": "concept", "title": "Research gaps"}], "description": "A literature review helps students enter a scholarly conversation rather than assemble disconnected summaries."}]}, {"id": "25f629af-dd92-4e24-8004-f50b5b94de58", "type": "topic", "title": "Research Ethics, IRB, Privacy, and Human Subjects Protection", "description": "Learn how to protect people, communities, records, and institutions while doing justice research.", "children": [{"id": "c0adc00d-e402-4a23-accd-0868b8a992ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Human subjects protection", "children": [{"id": "9f56b608-6fb6-4fa0-9c85-bf4a9f40be88", "type": "concept", "title": "Informed consent"}, {"id": "0c2729a5-c11e-4f67-85b6-e54207f4a22d", "type": "concept", "title": "Vulnerable populations"}, {"id": "a1c31d26-53a0-4bd1-92a7-5ee055532817", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality"}, {"id": "9bc73ba6-33d7-4415-a311-3e3f95f7b8ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk minimization"}], "description": "CJ research can expose participants to legal, social, emotional, or institutional risk."}, {"id": "147b92ab-7820-4ed9-8654-57da536cac75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IRB and research governance", "children": [{"id": "7f06dfb8-4b78-4609-9b7f-83ccb15b8b6b", "type": "concept", "title": "IRB protocols"}, {"id": "c2ed95f4-5723-42ac-a4e1-b5fcaa942461", "type": "concept", "title": "Exempt and expedited review"}, {"id": "029fe530-6e8e-4db8-9af7-fa114c12a5a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent forms"}, {"id": "bb3efcca-c697-4332-a0c6-ad47a82fed1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Data management plans"}], "description": "Students learn how ethical review works and why it matters before data collection begins."}, {"id": "daf69b2d-b835-4558-99e1-0a668d098a20", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Privacy and sensitive justice data", "children": [{"id": "6ecbb2a3-27f8-48d5-ba9b-d1e93a38a75f", "type": "concept", "title": "De-identification"}, {"id": "69134ca2-dee2-470c-93c5-ea5193032ebf", "type": "concept", "title": "Certificates of confidentiality"}, {"id": "94876bb2-e3f7-4985-88aa-2bc7f60cc083", "type": "concept", "title": "Secure storage"}, {"id": "d3e78574-dca4-4ea1-a723-71afaf08cdc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Data sharing limits"}], "description": "Justice data often involve victims, minors, defendants, incarcerated people, and confidential records."}]}, {"id": "d9474761-df3b-48cb-b919-7e8d3ea901dc", "type": "topic", "title": "Research Design Logic, Validity, and Inference", "description": "Understand how design choices determine what claims a study can credibly make.", "children": [{"id": "01b61dff-1e1d-47be-9e4c-9964f2563e2b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design choices", "children": [{"id": "e5a6556b-be83-4d94-b59c-c9e4b1a26481", "type": "concept", "title": "Units of analysis"}, {"id": "37bb7749-ae49-4bf2-a802-10d7b81ddc16", "type": "concept", "title": "Time ordering"}, {"id": "59e76acb-437e-4bd8-962e-ecb8d36076ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparison groups"}, {"id": "4e40039c-b166-472b-868b-5cde3a740936", "type": "concept", "title": "Case selection"}], "description": "Research design is the bridge between a question and a credible answer."}, {"id": "1ddabdaa-fdba-4c37-820f-fe60cda452e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Validity", "children": [{"id": "f67d8202-e147-43d3-acf4-8124b0d056fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal validity"}, {"id": "4467c1be-f0f7-44a9-8ec9-48b9d252c00d", "type": "concept", "title": "External validity"}, {"id": "ea611bd7-e26f-405b-ac85-78390d0e193e", "type": "concept", "title": "Construct validity"}, {"id": "3501c69d-acc4-4e42-b91c-f5d24613b08c", "type": "concept", "title": "Statistical conclusion validity"}], "description": "Validity teaches students to ask whether a study measures and explains what it claims."}, {"id": "f8c318d8-17ac-43f9-9dcf-069ebb76764d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Threats to inference", "children": [{"id": "88808b30-1654-4724-afa0-1ca24ba223ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Selection bias"}, {"id": "fcbc52c7-99bc-4d88-990f-13e26a459287", "type": "concept", "title": "Confounding"}, {"id": "78fa201c-0014-4025-b356-867287020784", "type": "concept", "title": "History and maturation"}, {"id": "34579ab4-50bb-4ab6-a634-1f94017397a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement error"}], "description": "Students learn to diagnose weaknesses before accepting research findings."}]}, {"id": "923a77bc-c169-4a5a-adc8-e363ffa475a2", "type": "topic", "title": "Measurement, Operationalization, Reliability, and Validity", "description": "Translate concepts such as crime, fear, recidivism, legitimacy, and disparity into defensible measures.", "children": [{"id": "73a8de85-b6ec-44db-aebc-2e4d93d2ea73", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Operationalization", "children": [{"id": "8480e8e8-1b8e-4236-acc0-f106212effb7", "type": "concept", "title": "Crime rates"}, {"id": "4db6f826-3fb2-46a7-a589-20a6e220adfb", "type": "concept", "title": "Recidivism"}, {"id": "ec416d5f-f071-4661-ab95-460b4384dbc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Fear of crime"}, {"id": "27730875-495e-4734-bade-301cd7e87653", "type": "concept", "title": "Police legitimacy"}], "description": "Operationalization turns abstract justice concepts into observable variables."}, {"id": "35c97980-d93a-4374-a4ee-517807969820", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reliability", "children": [{"id": "2a13a061-103d-4862-8ed9-87ba4d4e0bb6", "type": "concept", "title": "Interrater reliability"}, {"id": "db911a8a-68d0-481f-8dac-29155beb944c", "type": "concept", "title": "Test-retest reliability"}, {"id": "59337a06-2e8e-4f54-8f32-4220e4dc1cc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal consistency"}, {"id": "f3a6a696-9eae-4f0c-b112-00a5ee0b2479", "type": "concept", "title": "Coding rules"}], "description": "Reliable measurement produces consistent results across coders, instruments, or repeated measures."}, {"id": "46e5cef2-ca00-4da8-b467-54c72ba3e9a9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Measurement validity", "children": [{"id": "8c9c0770-51b3-4d1e-8830-b91b69aa329f", "type": "concept", "title": "Face validity"}, {"id": "ded2d121-e9a0-49cc-98c1-39b110e54e9f", "type": "concept", "title": "Content validity"}, {"id": "35d31545-baa0-4d54-8b42-4b8f18ba3af1", "type": "concept", "title": "Criterion validity"}, {"id": "d7a26b31-3ac2-4ce5-b3e4-5f3c8e3db017", "type": "concept", "title": "Construct validity"}], "description": "Valid measures capture the concept they are supposed to capture."}]}, {"id": "fb49a3b8-ec27-43a9-9fd7-7b9853929771", "type": "topic", "title": "Sampling, Populations, and Data Quality", "description": "Learn how sampling decisions shape representation, uncertainty, bias, and generalizability.", "children": [{"id": "1bc5334a-8f70-4336-9f2f-7c20c8d9de9e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Population and sampling frame", "children": [{"id": "973f9a42-9b18-471c-bc0b-c1a94d9d66d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Target population"}, {"id": "2162789a-5a04-4984-b606-3d2d112d1e29", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling frame"}, {"id": "92ec7e2a-f850-4ae2-96bc-cd355e03c471", "type": "concept", "title": "Units"}, {"id": "440b42f4-c0aa-4086-8d65-9a54bc913ee9", "type": "concept", "title": "Coverage error"}], "description": "Students must define who or what the study is about before selecting cases."}, {"id": "11c47dce-da25-409d-97df-2cbfabba5d7a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sampling strategies", "children": [{"id": "d921cd66-216c-4260-81bf-6046fd29f80d", "type": "concept", "title": "Probability sampling"}, {"id": "ec3553b0-2377-4b01-aa17-057730c4d520", "type": "concept", "title": "Stratified sampling"}, {"id": "edfa97f5-5a53-4369-95a9-3967d75ebe59", "type": "concept", "title": "Cluster sampling"}, {"id": "ead305e1-0766-4600-8896-823e8db344e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Purposive and snowball sampling"}], "description": "Sampling strategy shapes uncertainty, bias, cost, and feasibility."}, {"id": "2b80519e-60c0-4f62-9626-664776a00dd5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data quality", "children": [{"id": "cb0eff97-7db4-4be8-b0f8-c6bdfa0bede3", "type": "concept", "title": "Missing data"}, {"id": "a131ce0e-4609-4212-ad0e-7d82f624cdb7", "type": "concept", "title": "Nonresponse"}, {"id": "bc8b3e92-c32d-4332-9a26-2f6d1e271c5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Outliers"}, {"id": "d63c4f74-589a-4f6f-bce6-5b5ed2054f1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Data provenance"}], "description": "Justice data can be incomplete, biased, delayed, inconsistent, or shaped by policy and enforcement."}]}, {"id": "687eebe7-05bb-4881-9b83-7fce6992e0fb", "type": "topic", "title": "Surveys, Questionnaires, and Victimization Research", "description": "Design and evaluate surveys that measure behavior, attitudes, victimization, fear, and system experiences.", "children": [{"id": "ae38d11b-3ee2-44d0-bdad-6b2422950e0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Survey design", "children": [{"id": "df610457-4f67-4393-b9a4-fecc59f448ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Question wording"}, {"id": "a7333a5b-aa06-42cc-9975-d01a264912d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Response scales"}, {"id": "8e90b5a5-187a-49fd-a718-1eeaa7f4d744", "type": "concept", "title": "Question order"}, {"id": "d1bc8fc8-d38b-4ab7-ad37-96d4dcb3c0c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Pilot testing"}], "description": "Surveys work only when questions are clear, unbiased, ethical, and connected to constructs."}, {"id": "00f1869e-5595-4398-8209-fb9ae02f82a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Victimization research", "children": [{"id": "37c980bf-1238-471f-90a2-4986496c2f7e", "type": "concept", "title": "NCVS logic"}, {"id": "fa5d7dd9-9736-4cbe-a3cc-450d7da0da8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Recall period"}, {"id": "87f4d204-5dd7-4f0b-b278-8abe38be3820", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitive questions"}, {"id": "4a143655-7ec9-411a-9709-81880f16a52a", "type": "concept", "title": "Underreporting"}], "description": "Victimization surveys reveal harms that official police data often miss."}, {"id": "e18b149f-c5d4-4714-aa98-353148dda7bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Survey implementation", "children": [{"id": "9d1dcdf0-2ac1-4af0-b8ac-187c2b326931", "type": "concept", "title": "Modes of survey delivery"}, {"id": "6cdd83ce-1a4a-459c-b322-b3c592acaad4", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling weights"}, {"id": "f0ed72dc-cc1e-4ede-946f-b8585b3313b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Nonresponse bias"}, {"id": "043da81d-b8fe-4a2a-b9ee-98e46870e4ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency reports"}], "description": "Administration choices affect response rates and data quality."}]}, {"id": "a961734a-9eaf-4d33-b3df-27ab189e411d", "type": "topic", "title": "Qualitative Interviews, Focus Groups, and Ethnography", "description": "Use qualitative methods to study meaning, process, discretion, culture, and lived experience in justice settings.", "children": [{"id": "80020f63-f072-40cc-b2c0-b1cd4bb24dce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interview methods", "children": [{"id": "fe4f287e-07eb-499c-aea3-dde9a6c3cf83", "type": "concept", "title": "Structured interviews"}, {"id": "57a18846-cb1b-44f0-8bcc-cf6b19e61cc2", "type": "concept", "title": "Semi-structured interviews"}, {"id": "e26fc973-e187-45fc-a3a0-ce576202a0b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Elite interviews"}, {"id": "71ea506c-0c76-421e-8fbf-0de18c1bafd2", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed interviewing"}], "description": "Interviews reveal meanings, experiences, strategies, and perceptions that datasets may flatten."}, {"id": "db111ab7-8c85-4e20-b004-69f0554db13d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Focus groups", "children": [{"id": "81729b6b-2827-4712-a7c3-8155ccddf41f", "type": "concept", "title": "Recruitment"}, {"id": "19ed4938-6990-4289-bde9-860f4644cc61", "type": "concept", "title": "Moderator guides"}, {"id": "2dad97c3-c8ec-4789-9a12-f26fa24e3e11", "type": "concept", "title": "Group dynamics"}, {"id": "ac537b0e-f19a-415b-b8e1-99956b7cd74c", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality limits"}], "description": "Focus groups help researchers study group meaning-making and community perspectives."}, {"id": "5a5e9dcf-08dd-4490-b81d-e4a8de5cb8a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethnography", "children": [{"id": "ca889737-9bb8-4616-9ecb-fb0c2f537157", "type": "concept", "title": "Participant observation"}, {"id": "43b21575-5acb-40fb-be0a-25555cb9cf18", "type": "concept", "title": "Field notes"}, {"id": "fceb6778-a63d-4d10-90ac-94f64e6f68cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflexivity"}, {"id": "59980559-9918-47cb-896e-6713ff06b300", "type": "concept", "title": "Access and trust"}], "description": "Ethnography helps students study institutional culture and daily practice in context."}]}, {"id": "21d1b1d7-5040-4efa-9d60-49cb14c6bc13", "type": "topic", "title": "Field Observation, Case Studies, and Court or Agency Research", "description": "Study justice organizations in context through observation, case analysis, field notes, and institutional access.", "children": [{"id": "28e6a817-eaef-4f9b-80fa-fb88be4e85e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Observation", "children": [{"id": "2a3fdd57-bf99-45b7-b5fa-73647236d25d", "type": "concept", "title": "Court watching"}, {"id": "3ee7987a-394a-4f60-a8aa-e2b07d55dc92", "type": "concept", "title": "Ride-alongs"}, {"id": "e9c6f6e9-eb73-4956-91bb-2bf8029e08b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency meetings"}, {"id": "866f203a-4e46-4fd4-8fcb-bb73ce50ed1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Systematic observation instruments"}], "description": "Observation teaches students to connect official rules to lived institutional practice."}, {"id": "37fdd093-7d26-47b7-b2f6-2151ac2f39e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case studies", "children": [{"id": "edd5a5c5-d312-4604-9458-da4b7681363a", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-case design"}, {"id": "974b2202-6e10-4d28-b147-603334c164be", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative case study"}, {"id": "e8ecd600-ba9c-46d8-9b99-d3fe42ec033e", "type": "concept", "title": "Process tracing"}, {"id": "75815317-83aa-4c10-a338-f1641361f6a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Document analysis"}], "description": "Case studies provide depth for understanding policy implementation, organizations, and unusual events."}, {"id": "04b1ea72-dde2-4d4f-a867-39e109b5d1a2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutional access", "children": [{"id": "53f6121f-5e4a-4e86-b3e3-3c4fbca565bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Memoranda of understanding"}, {"id": "52103235-70d9-499a-9b35-1aa1e83348e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Gatekeepers"}, {"id": "1eb6a6e8-ca07-4c92-ae08-667ef5f51e24", "type": "concept", "title": "Researcher safety"}, {"id": "b3ac7541-fb65-4758-af51-4fb83d0ca84b", "type": "concept", "title": "Role clarity"}], "description": "Research in justice agencies requires planning, permissions, trust, and boundary management."}]}, {"id": "38bf2abe-008a-4724-b886-e78f6f2e2d53", "type": "topic", "title": "Experiments, Quasi-Experiments, and Program Evaluation", "description": "Evaluate interventions and policies using designs that strengthen causal inference while respecting ethics and feasibility.", "children": [{"id": "7de72e2c-b1f1-41a6-a1d4-ffebc8b82fce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Experiments", "children": [{"id": "7c41fe42-9d46-4479-8447-1ef324ee7fdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Random assignment"}, {"id": "8d867acf-3e68-4a4c-b05e-629065aac91c", "type": "concept", "title": "Treatment and control"}, {"id": "de1e7e2c-614d-4b1b-b780-e66933200f66", "type": "concept", "title": "Field experiments"}, {"id": "6d47b053-fdf1-48c6-bdc5-e565456bdf61", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation fidelity"}], "description": "Experiments can estimate causal effects when random assignment is ethical and feasible."}, {"id": "d015c497-3320-4979-93d6-c0e6e8f1de2e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quasi-experiments", "children": [{"id": "a2f0a040-19dc-463d-be44-ee428b9cff56", "type": "concept", "title": "Difference-in-differences"}, {"id": "867fbd80-ba07-4927-a7a4-be15bddc2112", "type": "concept", "title": "Regression discontinuity"}, {"id": "2e4c6dd4-9c21-41f2-9385-619b2bb0a7b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Matching"}, {"id": "799cd451-c312-451e-997f-c8bd54bdf322", "type": "concept", "title": "Interrupted time series"}], "description": "Quasi-experimental designs strengthen causal claims when randomization is not possible."}, {"id": "4ab1616d-0c3c-490c-9899-32fc4734003f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Program evaluation", "children": [{"id": "11a44abf-2e95-4262-b62a-eb55d9c0c343", "type": "concept", "title": "Logic models"}, {"id": "dfb3d481-8004-4fa7-81c9-a5cc5d4f8a4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Process evaluation"}, {"id": "d51a8f9c-faee-410e-913c-b30ae4d35398", "type": "concept", "title": "Outcome evaluation"}, {"id": "c3c5125c-c19e-4546-8420-f6ab42d1adb9", "type": "concept", "title": "Impact evaluation"}], "description": "Evaluation connects research methods to practical questions about whether programs work."}]}, {"id": "cb20d315-d4a1-4d38-9c7f-9766e88b639f", "type": "topic", "title": "Official Criminal Justice Data and Administrative Records", "description": "Use UCR, NIBRS, NCVS, BJS, court, corrections, and agency records with care and skepticism.", "children": [{"id": "4e134ee2-e19a-42eb-b1b6-d28dd2ca90c4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crime data systems", "children": [{"id": "b53e900f-1465-41f9-ae75-5d90e8e4db8c", "type": "concept", "title": "UCR"}, {"id": "83479786-8c3f-44ca-9f2f-3158906bc248", "type": "concept", "title": "NIBRS"}, {"id": "3acccf70-652e-4c96-b905-33b82d131234", "type": "concept", "title": "FBI Crime Data Explorer"}, {"id": "fd54ff12-8dba-41e0-89b1-8d1ee5bc9b74", "type": "concept", "title": "Clearance data"}], "description": "Official data are powerful but reflect reporting, recording, and enforcement practices."}, {"id": "87151277-71df-480c-b211-9a4e2f744298", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Victimization and justice datasets", "children": [{"id": "e32cf32e-cb99-4e10-96f9-41df22fd2d9a", "type": "concept", "title": "NCVS"}, {"id": "c4f92c87-ad16-4852-9c2e-12da6fe5515f", "type": "concept", "title": "NACJD"}, {"id": "30440a09-0a6e-4a8e-874b-414bbffe1b98", "type": "concept", "title": "BJS Data Analysis Tools"}, {"id": "c7a36028-e060-4239-b9ec-794c81ef4d97", "type": "concept", "title": "Court and corrections datasets"}], "description": "Students learn to find and interpret major public datasets."}, {"id": "a2f98426-4b7f-4fc7-aba1-2611b8b64e95", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Administrative data cautions", "children": [{"id": "830b7ff9-6b99-4a4c-9cac-dad7c725c889", "type": "concept", "title": "Changing definitions"}, {"id": "e7e12b76-5f30-47a4-9a45-4ef4738b5525", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency incentives"}, {"id": "8ae7d336-c585-4687-a188-a51de6dc3789", "type": "concept", "title": "Record linkage"}, {"id": "987ba89e-1cc1-4fb9-8ee4-e3961cb36ea8", "type": "concept", "title": "Data dictionaries"}], "description": "Administrative records are collected for operations, not always for research."}]}, {"id": "f8351417-84a8-48d9-9493-d12f97717fe6", "type": "topic", "title": "Descriptive Statistics and Exploratory Data Analysis", "description": "Summarize justice data clearly before moving to complex inference or policy claims.", "children": [{"id": "dcdb265a-dfe5-473c-82f1-fbb379814b3a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Describing distributions", "children": [{"id": "b517be1c-4249-4d75-a3c6-fe785b0dc343", "type": "concept", "title": "Frequencies"}, {"id": "fe739b22-51cc-426b-8ec4-ebc6b0eebb82", "type": "concept", "title": "Means and medians"}, {"id": "3a1e3b02-70f0-4a8f-822f-e0d62901a6bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Variation"}, {"id": "e62a90f2-f95c-44ec-bc36-c72e3bd20e77", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-tabulations"}], "description": "Exploration helps students understand what the data say before testing claims."}, {"id": "9b5dce6b-bb6c-4df5-98fb-be2312331043", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visualization", "children": [{"id": "7b12e814-855d-4d38-8689-a4f48439fbf0", "type": "concept", "title": "Bar charts"}, {"id": "1c2b7939-433b-472a-8125-229d0df60ad1", "type": "concept", "title": "Line charts"}, {"id": "e3ffe359-64d1-4030-b5e1-48551ceb40e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Maps"}, {"id": "d8e375c3-4861-4b8e-b87a-0c049d32a44b", "type": "concept", "title": "Rates and denominators"}], "description": "Good graphics reveal patterns, comparisons, and uncertainty without misleading the reader."}, {"id": "6f46c8c8-58b3-4a2b-99e3-bb53b1888680", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data cleaning", "children": [{"id": "363f2740-851a-433a-814f-67055c251417", "type": "concept", "title": "Missing values"}, {"id": "174769a0-8a64-495d-bda0-42adaa5749e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Duplicate cases"}, {"id": "3b108aed-c788-439f-b6ee-7283571c280c", "type": "concept", "title": "Recoding"}, {"id": "c03edc0e-ace0-4709-9200-4c97779ab9df", "type": "concept", "title": "Audit trails"}], "description": "Data analysis begins with careful checking and documentation."}]}, {"id": "7e2e8333-6302-4f87-a9ca-1fb3141c5fbe", "type": "topic", "title": "Hypothesis Testing, Association, and Group Comparisons", "description": "Use inferential tools to compare groups, estimate uncertainty, and test empirical claims.", "children": [{"id": "541e3726-65e0-4074-8044-4b0be293b128", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inference foundations", "children": [{"id": "aeea24b4-2f92-4456-8916-a006a34b9af6", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling distributions"}, {"id": "159d40fe-cedc-4452-a8ea-02a8bf4602f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidence intervals"}, {"id": "bb403558-0d6d-4fb9-a810-62f8b9856c7f", "type": "concept", "title": "p-values"}, {"id": "496470db-db94-4964-83be-12a30e581a1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Statistical significance"}], "description": "Inference helps students distinguish patterns in data from random variation."}, {"id": "7bc7426a-80c9-4e50-a9c1-03fa9e2fe12a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Group comparisons", "children": [{"id": "035b3c6b-85a1-43d7-ba9d-e3242b28b2cb", "type": "concept", "title": "t-tests"}, {"id": "d6ff9b60-6255-45ea-8b72-8f92e4837bec", "type": "concept", "title": "ANOVA"}, {"id": "40b576d6-cf1b-47e1-a9df-591900eb2a2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Chi-square"}, {"id": "64c766b6-7ef4-44d9-ae5e-cc6ec6f1b8b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Effect sizes"}], "description": "CJ research often compares outcomes across groups, places, programs, or time periods."}, {"id": "6f8f2ea1-175d-45e8-b319-272174e5a6bb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Association", "children": [{"id": "1ffa54a2-e0df-45ff-a2f0-193e04d7c4ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Correlation"}, {"id": "712e1998-502b-40ac-b842-f98fefb60c21", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-tabs"}, {"id": "bb148c02-ff69-485e-8ec8-e9cb577b11fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk ratios"}, {"id": "ed76ef22-909b-4824-a24e-592a5cdd8e95", "type": "concept", "title": "Odds ratios overview"}], "description": "Association tools show whether variables move together, while reminding students that association is not causation."}]}, {"id": "b9e6b41a-d11b-42b4-b582-95c5e10f975b", "type": "topic", "title": "Regression, Prediction, and Introductory Causal Inference", "description": "Use multivariate models to study relationships, prediction, controls, and causal designs without overclaiming.", "children": [{"id": "1769a285-16d3-4538-bcf2-824cc6358a5f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regression basics", "children": [{"id": "9533465a-0b9d-455c-b7ab-ea5e4686019a", "type": "concept", "title": "Simple regression"}, {"id": "81c6d68e-323b-46c9-90f8-76d4c944020e", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple regression"}, {"id": "8596ef53-4656-4d70-9bef-968a995b9840", "type": "concept", "title": "Logistic regression awareness"}, {"id": "a095c4be-0ce3-4891-89ad-b9e5b1ccb3f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Model assumptions"}], "description": "Regression helps summarize relationships while adjusting for measured covariates."}, {"id": "43e43fbb-67d2-437c-8dc9-cac6c1f48f8e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prediction vs causal inference", "children": [{"id": "798d98d4-0589-4318-a1c7-1a25896f34c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Training and testing"}, {"id": "84a7f8a5-ab20-4822-b669-ca5c8c4c07da", "type": "concept", "title": "Confounding"}, {"id": "ba4c6cd8-4091-4567-b15d-d69edff5cbb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Counterfactuals"}, {"id": "9619180f-e95b-4d82-b8c2-6c635f527ec7", "type": "concept", "title": "External validity"}], "description": "Students learn the difference between predicting outcomes and estimating effects."}, {"id": "cde17373-d485-441e-b1e6-a79498231dc1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible interpretation", "children": [{"id": "c97286fa-c151-485f-9b52-487a3ec421bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Coefficients"}, {"id": "fee97a05-e4ca-4c7b-9f9f-57a53b99d3e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Predicted values"}, {"id": "c61a61c9-5c4f-462f-a694-dd7ffdbcc4a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Robustness checks"}, {"id": "95c56a6c-bfdd-4ac0-9fff-abc4b097ae26", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding causal overclaiming"}], "description": "Models must be interpreted with humility, context, uncertainty, and limitations."}]}, {"id": "b6f9de1a-bc7f-4431-97f6-345f5fb266d5", "type": "topic", "title": "Mixed Methods, Triangulation, and Evidence Synthesis", "description": "Combine qualitative, quantitative, and administrative evidence to answer richer criminal justice questions.", "children": [{"id": "25290e0f-2b00-4003-954e-3acf55eefd21", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Why mix methods", "children": [{"id": "2cc18a30-3a79-4b62-be86-9604e26761b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Complementarity"}, {"id": "af5d1803-4d2c-4d2e-b3b0-115dc62139ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Triangulation"}, {"id": "b0779126-e77f-4632-8a38-2136ea6b70d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Mechanisms"}, {"id": "944c03fd-5835-466b-bcd9-8b6e42ba7526", "type": "concept", "title": "Context"}], "description": "Mixed methods help answer questions that need both breadth and depth."}, {"id": "373cf166-b41b-492f-a1c2-d0a626fbee28", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mixed-method designs", "children": [{"id": "ee163493-bfa0-42f8-b34f-20423274a84b", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequential explanatory"}, {"id": "0a1f6038-e5eb-4b09-bf25-c1a5b08ad856", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequential exploratory"}, {"id": "375e3401-a683-478d-b85c-f88f9358adfc", "type": "concept", "title": "Convergent design"}, {"id": "e2b5bfc6-df66-4e3d-9997-821241b8eab9", "type": "concept", "title": "Embedded design"}], "description": "Students learn common ways to sequence and integrate methods."}, {"id": "62d8579e-514d-4cac-8ebe-5815a0e9870b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence synthesis", "children": [{"id": "ae6fd732-6fea-4fd3-bb53-cf546eed7422", "type": "concept", "title": "Systematic reviews"}, {"id": "eafaee0c-0711-4b1c-916e-b195cc3d948d", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence grading"}, {"id": "fd576ec9-9ead-4bea-867c-20ae0f69889b", "type": "concept", "title": "CrimeSolutions examples"}, {"id": "57e57427-d603-4b58-97b2-7c6b1da7a936", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy memos"}], "description": "Synthesis teaches students to evaluate bodies of evidence, not just single studies."}]}, {"id": "5e3dfd4c-f443-4a46-8296-f97e194245e8", "type": "topic", "title": "Reproducible Workflow, Statistical Software, and Documentation", "description": "Build transparent workflows using codebooks, project folders, software, versioning, and reproducible analysis habits.", "children": [{"id": "24569f3a-ed59-4f7c-a6d8-1bf178c6d418", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project workflow", "children": [{"id": "bc0b173a-a0b8-41b3-89c9-4ace2b4963bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Folder structure"}, {"id": "20ced5b2-f525-4bc0-8dca-9d0173f07560", "type": "concept", "title": "File naming"}, {"id": "33716988-3654-4199-ad9f-5979d59733a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Version control"}, {"id": "0862befb-50c5-494d-9bd9-ca90dc0f7f6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Research logs"}], "description": "A good workflow makes research understandable, rerunnable, and easier to improve."}, {"id": "9c2aebdf-c193-47ff-9bc9-3b3bab9c1e2e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Statistical software", "children": [{"id": "d153b093-71a5-4a3b-aa28-a26087278f5e", "type": "concept", "title": "SPSS"}, {"id": "db597954-3059-45c5-9f47-d3e01744e355", "type": "concept", "title": "R"}, {"id": "58920e5e-ea3a-47b4-aed5-770a3cdccc75", "type": "concept", "title": "Python"}, {"id": "8fa2a324-3f92-4bd7-bfd6-90bec16174d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Notebooks and scripts"}], "description": "Students should gain practical analysis habits in tools used for justice research."}, {"id": "c1402fd9-53a3-49b8-83f7-52289533a453", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentation", "children": [{"id": "240ac67f-647b-4b64-af90-fce093722025", "type": "concept", "title": "Codebooks"}, {"id": "a1d837f2-9c79-414c-b7ed-e071cefb54be", "type": "concept", "title": "Metadata"}, {"id": "85b4adec-b99f-4496-b745-b05199a602fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Syntax files"}, {"id": "27453373-c745-46ee-806f-d0d31a821fec", "type": "concept", "title": "Replication packages"}], "description": "Documentation makes research inspectable by instructors, teammates, agencies, and future readers."}]}, {"id": "8f4d7b11-3fc1-43d7-b37d-2baa37009c3b", "type": "topic", "title": "Equity, Bias, Data Justice, and Responsible Analytics", "description": "Identify how measurement, sampling, algorithms, privacy, and institutional data can reproduce or challenge injustice.", "children": [{"id": "621712f8-2146-49aa-9237-901d15ea704b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bias in research systems", "children": [{"id": "95e39ce6-40a0-4aa0-a8aa-dc7ae434c7bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Selection bias"}, {"id": "52b66e71-b7c7-4aa2-8587-e8b7cee71c2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement bias"}, {"id": "05120ee2-4168-495f-aa74-0be22700100c", "type": "concept", "title": "Algorithmic bias"}, {"id": "18a85873-a9e1-4854-871e-7d67aef3bb1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Publication bias"}], "description": "Bias can enter through questions, samples, measures, models, and interpretation."}, {"id": "b1fe1de7-c2ba-4e38-9f5d-5291bd64aec6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equity-centered analysis", "children": [{"id": "0bf62077-292e-4263-aa8d-f26c67859433", "type": "concept", "title": "Disaggregation"}, {"id": "f029562e-d10f-4d1f-b4e7-8f10ec695acc", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersectionality"}, {"id": "784bfc4d-04c9-40a6-beff-d90a8b1af5af", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity metrics"}, {"id": "71ee36dd-65de-46dc-afb8-97bfb92a91e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Contextual interpretation"}], "description": "Equity analysis asks who benefits, who is harmed, and what disparities appear across decision points."}, {"id": "5aacf3d4-4cb7-490d-92ef-f82302043c84", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible analytics", "children": [{"id": "cbc3921e-1e56-4f59-b4ef-a80057f2661a", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy protection"}, {"id": "086e33b1-9017-4d27-b7e7-434b557932cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Data governance"}, {"id": "2471744f-33c8-439f-bf9e-0a161465acc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Model transparency"}, {"id": "148857ac-e221-48ed-b791-a435b7be1867", "type": "concept", "title": "Community accountability"}], "description": "Responsible analytics balances public safety, rights, privacy, fairness, and transparency."}]}, {"id": "1cb3f089-8e6d-4895-b938-4e0b9cffde1e", "type": "topic", "title": "Research Reports, Visualization, Presentation, and Capstone Proposal", "description": "Communicate methods, findings, limitations, and recommendations in professional research reports and presentations.", "children": [{"id": "da8ba19c-6288-457d-b764-59489c635f13", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research reporting", "children": [{"id": "695cebf7-4369-4d86-8fc3-6d09d10a1eb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Abstract"}, {"id": "0e31a022-6047-4332-b8d4-86d506152433", "type": "concept", "title": "Methods section"}, {"id": "1ef1b46f-96d4-4e0b-9398-43b4c5956f93", "type": "concept", "title": "Results"}, {"id": "02f384a0-5ba7-4edd-abc1-e8450f9884c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Limitations"}], "description": "Research reports turn methods and evidence into a transparent argument."}, {"id": "67d8f377-eb62-418a-b8f9-73ce15453657", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visualization and presentation", "children": [{"id": "5f5a2bd6-ee62-4073-9ea4-d57cd9e9505b", "type": "concept", "title": "Tables"}, {"id": "6127658b-c9c3-4527-b300-04a9c919741e", "type": "concept", "title": "Figures"}, {"id": "7913d262-c830-4cff-bbeb-ace34e3d3643", "type": "concept", "title": "Slide briefing"}, {"id": "cff4ada6-eb21-4ca1-b9af-bf3bfc08816c", "type": "concept", "title": "Plain-language summary"}], "description": "Students learn to explain findings to scholarly, agency, and public audiences."}, {"id": "28a7caec-bd4b-4d39-9ab6-c3a1706d6f78", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capstone proposal", "children": [{"id": "8c4cc155-75ff-4195-9cef-671d6858bbfc", "type": "concept", "title": "Research question"}, {"id": "83244317-a006-4d81-a48e-e86d5720f2de", "type": "concept", "title": "Literature review"}, {"id": "a13df1d9-9a6f-4e18-be4c-638af522f7fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Methods plan"}, {"id": "aeb73cbb-3b76-412b-bd6e-2f5fa600084c", "type": "concept", "title": "Timeline and feasibility"}], "description": "The capstone proposal integrates question, literature, design, ethics, data, analysis, and expected contribution."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$rmcjjson$::jsonb,
