": "Theory and conceptual framing", "children": [{"id": "50cc9ee9-2f09-4402-9516-4afea565f306", "type": "concept", "title": "Criminological theory"}, {"id": "c0b3b592-e282-4fcd-8fe5-887353d7ef61", "type": "concept", "title": "Organizational theory"}, {"id": "efeb61fa-6e1b-4d50-8196-be6163aad6d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Procedural justice"}, {"id": "45b56c44-23e9-4c9a-9b72-1f50e1f3ac18", "type": "concept", "title": "Deterrence and opportunity"}], "description": "Theory explains why a justice outcome might occur and what mechanisms link causes to effects."}, {"id": "00643cf7-2bd0-447a-be60-4ec14a2904e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Literature review", "children": [{"id": "3103a67d-47df-4a3a-9b35-81266c806d38", "type": "concept", "title": "Search strategies"}, {"id": "a8de72d4-7c4a-4daf-9cd6-5b431d51cb3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Source quality"}, {"id": "6915e36f-2204-44d2-b40b-edffb9e6d6e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Synthesis"}, {"id": "8b39f1be-2083-48b5-9d71-208ab012bf70", "type": "concept", "title": "Research gaps"}], "description": "A literature review helps students enter a scholarly conversation rather than assemble disconnected summaries."}]}, {"id": "25f629af-dd92-4e24-8004-f50b5b94de58", "type": "topic", "title": "Research Ethics, IRB, Privacy, and Human Subjects Protection", "description": "Learn how to protect people, communities, records, and institutions while doing justice research.", "children": [{"id": "c0adc00d-e402-4a23-accd-0868b8a992ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Human subjects protection", "children": [{"id": "9f56b608-6fb6-4fa0-9c85-bf4a9f40be88", "type": "concept", "title": "Informed consent"}, {"id": "0c2729a5-c11e-4f67-85b6-e54207f4a22d", "type": "concept", "title": "Vulnerable populations"}, {"id": "a1c31d26-53a0-4bd1-92a7-5ee055532817", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality"}, {"id": "9bc73ba6-33d7-4415-a311-3e3f95f7b8ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk minimization"}], "description": "CJ research can expose participants to legal, social, emotional, or institutional risk."}, {"id": "147b92ab-7820-4ed9-8654-57da536cac75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IRB and research governance", "children": [{"id": "7f06dfb8-4b78-4609-9b7f-83ccb15b8b6b", "type": "concept", "title": "IRB protocols"}, {"id": "c2ed95f4-5723-42ac-a4e1-b5fcaa942461", "type": "concept", "title": "Exempt and expedited review"}, {"id": "029fe530-6e8e-4db8-9af7-fa114c12a5a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent forms"}, {"id": "bb3efcca-c697-4332-a0c6-ad47a82fed1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Data management plans"}], "description": "Students learn how ethical review works and why it matters before data collection begins."}, {"id": "daf69b2d-b835-4558-99e1-0a668d098a20", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Privacy and sensitive justice data", "children": [{"id": "6ecbb2a3-27f8-48d5-ba9b-d1e93a38a75f", "type": "concept", "title": "De-identification"}, {"id": "69134ca2-dee2-470c-93c5-ea5193032ebf", "type": "concept", "title": "Certificates of confidentiality"}, {"id": "94876bb2-e3f7-4985-88aa-2bc7f60cc083", "type": "concept", "title": "Secure storage"}, {"id": "d3e78574-dca4-4ea1-a723-71afaf08cdc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Data sharing limits"}], "description": "Justice data often involve victims, minors, defendants, incarcerated people, and confidential records."}]}, {"id": "d9474761-df3b-48cb-b919-7e8d3ea901dc", "type": "topic", "title": "Research Design Logic, Validity, and Inference", "description": "Understand how design choices determine what claims a study can credibly make.", "children": [{"id": "01b61dff-1e1d-47be-9e4c-9964f2563e2b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design choices", "children": [{"id": "e5a6556b-be83-4d94-b59c-c9e4b1a26481", "type": "concept", "title": "Units of analysis"}, {"id": "37bb7749-ae49-4bf2-a802-10d7b81ddc16", "type": "concept", "title": "Time ordering"}, {"id": "59e76acb-437e-4bd8-962e-ecb8d36076ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparison groups"}, {"id": "4e40039c-b166-472b-868b-5cde3a740936", "type": "concept", "title": "Case selection"}], "description": "Research design is the bridge between a question and a credible answer."}, {"id": "1ddabdaa-fdba-4c37-820f-fe60cda452e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Validity", "children": [{"id": "f67d8202-e147-43d3-acf4-8124b0d056fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal validity"}, {"id": "4467c1be-f0f7-44a9-8ec9-48b9d252c00d", "type": "concept", "title": "External validity"}, {"id": "ea611bd7-e26f-405b-ac85-78390d0e193e", "type": "concept", "title": "Construct validity"}, {"id": "3501c69d-acc4-4e42-b91c-f5d24613b08c", "type": "concept", "title": "Statistical conclusion validity"}], "description": "Validity teaches students to ask whether a study measures and explains what it claims."}, {"id": "f8c318d8-17ac-43f9-9dcf-069ebb76764d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Threats to inference", "children": [{"id": "88808b30-1654-4724-afa0-1ca24ba223ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Selection bias"}, {"id": "fcbc52c7-99bc-4d88-990f-13e26a459287", "type": "concept", "title": "Confounding"}, {"id": "78fa201c-0014-4025-b356-867287020784", "type": "concept", "title": "History and maturation"}, {"id": "34579ab4-50bb-4ab6-a634-1f94017397a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement error"}], "description": "Students learn to diagnose weaknesses before accepting research findings."}]}, {"id": "923a77bc-c169-4a5a-adc8-e363ffa475a2", "type": "topic", "title": "Measurement, Operationalization, Reliability, and Validity", "description": "Translate concepts such as crime, fear, recidivism, legitimacy, and disparity into defensible measures.", "children": [{"id": "73a8de85-b6ec-44db-aebc-2e4d93d2ea73", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Operationalization", "children": [{"id": "8480e8e8-1b8e-4236-acc0-f106212effb7", "type": "concept", "title": "Crime rates"}, {"id": "4db6f826-3fb2-46a7-a589-20a6e220adfb", "type": "concept", "title": "Recidivism"}, {"id": "ec416d5f-f071-4661-ab95-460b4384dbc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Fear of crime"}, {"id": "27730875-495e-4734-bade-301cd7e87653", "type": "concept", "title": "Police legitimacy"}], "description": "Operationalization turns abstract justice concepts into observable variables."}, {"id": "35c97980-d93a-4374-a4ee-517807969820", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reliability", "children": [{"id": "2a13a061-103d-4862-8ed9-87ba4d4e0bb6", "type": "concept", "title": "Interrater reliability"}, {"id": "db911a8a-68d0-481f-8dac-29155beb944c", "type": "concept", "title": "Test-retest reliability"}, {"id": "59337a06-2e8e-4f54-8f32-4220e4dc1cc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal consistency"}, {"id": "f3a6a696-9eae-4f0c-b112-00a5ee0b2479", "type": "concept", "title": "Coding rules"}], "description": "Reliable measurement produces consistent results across coders, instruments, or repeated measures."}, {"id": "46e5cef2-ca00-4da8-b467-54c72ba3e9a9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Measurement validity", "children": [{"id": "8c9c0770-51b3-4d1e-8830-b91b69aa329f", "type": "concept", "title": "Face validity"}, {"id": "ded2d121-e9a0-49cc-98c1-39b110e54e9f", "type": "concept", "title": "Content validity"}, {"id": "35d31545-baa0-4d54-8b42-4b8f18ba3af1", "type": "concept", "title": "Criterion validity"}, {"id": "d7a26b31-3ac2-4ce5-b3e4-5f3c8e3db017", "type": "concept", "title": "Construct validity"}], "description": "Valid measures capture the concept they are supposed to capture."}]}, {"id": "fb49a3b8-ec27-43a9-9fd7-7b9853929771", "type": "topic", "title": "Sampling, Populations, and Data Quality", "description": "Learn how sampling decisions shape representation, uncertainty, bias, and generalizability.", "children": [{"id": "1bc5334a-8f70-4336-9f2f-7c20c8d9de9e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Population and sampling frame", "children": [{"id": "973f9a42-9b18-471c-bc0b-c1a94d9d66d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Target population"}, {"id": "2162789a-5a04-4984-b606-3d2d112d1e29", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling frame"}, {"id": "92ec7e2a-f850-4ae2-96bc-cd355e03c471", "type": "concept", "title": "Units"}, {"id": "440b42f4-c0aa-4086-8d65-9a54bc913ee9", "type": "concept", "title": "Coverage error"}], "description": "Students must define who or what the study is about before selecting cases."}, {"id": "11c47dce-da25-409d-97df-2cbfabba5d7a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sampling strategies", "children": [{"id": "d921cd66-216c-4260-81bf-6046fd29f80d", "type": "concept", "title": "Probability sampling"}, {"id": "ec3553b0-2377-4b01-aa17-057730c4d520", "type": "concept", "title": "Stratified sampling"}, {"id": "edfa97f5-5a53-4369-95a9-3967d75ebe59", "type": "concept", "title": "Cluster sampling"}, {"id": "ead305e1-0766-4600-8896-823e8db344e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Purposive and snowball sampling"}], "description": "Sampling strategy shapes uncertainty, bias, cost, and feasibility."}, {"id": "2b80519e-60c0-4f62-9626-664776a00dd5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data quality", "children": [{"id": "cb0eff97-7db4-4be8-b0f8-c6bdfa0bede3", "type": "concept", "title": "Missing data"}, {"id": "a131ce0e-4609-4212-ad0e-7d82f624cdb7", "type": "concept", "title": "Nonresponse"}, {"id": "bc8b3e92-c32d-4332-9a26-2f6d1e271c5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Outliers"}, {"id": "d63c4f74-589a-4f6f-bce6-5b5ed2054f1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Data provenance"}], "description": "Justice data can be incomplete, biased, delayed, inconsistent, or shaped by policy and enforcement."}]}, {"id": "687eebe7-05bb-4881-9b83-7fce6992e0fb", "type": "topic", "title": "Surveys, Questionnaires, and Victimization Research", "description": "Design and evaluate surveys that measure behavior, attitudes, victimization, fear, and system experiences.", "children": [{"id": "ae38d11b-3ee2-44d0-bdad-6b2422950e0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Survey design", "children": [{"id": "df610457-4f67-4393-b9a4-fecc59f448ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Question wording"}, {"id": "a7333a5b-aa06-42cc-9975-d01a264912d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Response scales"}, {"id": "8e90b5a5-187a-49fd-a718-1eeaa7f4d744", "type": "concept", "title": "Question order"}, {"id": "d1bc8fc8-d38b-4ab7-ad37-96d4dcb3c0c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Pilot testing"}], "description": "Surveys work only when questions are clear, unbiased, ethical, and connected to constructs."}, {"id": "00f1869e-5595-4398-8209-fb9ae02f82a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Victimization research", "children": [{"id": "37c980bf-1238-471f-90a2-4986496c2f7e", "type": "concept", "title": "NCVS logic"}, {"id": "fa5d7dd9-9736-4cbe-a3cc-450d7da0da8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Recall period"}, {"id": "87f4d204-5dd7-4f0b-b278-8abe38be3820", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitive questions"}, {"id": "4a143655-7ec9-411a-9709-81880f16a52a", "type": "concept", "title": "Underreporting"}], "description": "Victimization surveys reveal harms that official police data often miss."}, {"id": "e18b149f-c5d4-4714-aa98-353148dda7bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Survey implementation", "children": [{"id": "9d1dcdf0-2ac1-4af0-b8ac-187c2b326931", "type": "concept", "title": "Modes of survey delivery"}, {"id": "6cdd83ce-1a4a-459c-b322-b3c592acaad4", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling weights"}, {"id": "f0ed72dc-cc1e-4ede-946f-b8585b3313b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Nonresponse bias"}, {"id": "043da81d-b8fe-4a2a-b9ee-98e46870e4ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency reports"}], "description": "Administration choices affect response rates and data quality."}]}, {"id": "a961734a-9eaf-4d33-b3df-27ab189e411d", "type": "topic", "title": "Qualitative Interviews, Focus Groups, and Ethnography", "description": "Use qualitative methods to study meaning, process, discretion, culture, and lived experience in justice settings.", "children": [{"id": "80020f63-f072-40cc-b2c0-b1cd4bb24dce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interview methods", "children": [{"id": "fe4f287e-07eb-499c-aea3-dde9a6c3cf83", "type": "concept", "title": "Structured interviews"}, {"id": "57a18846-cb1b-44f0-8bcc-cf6b19e61cc2", "type": "concept", "title": "Semi-structured interviews"}, {"id": "e26fc973-e187-45fc-a3a0-ce576202a0b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Elite interviews"}, {"id": "71ea506c-0c76-421e-8fbf-0de18c1bafd2", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed interviewing"}], "description": "Interviews reveal meanings, experiences, strategies, and perceptions that datasets may flatten."}, {"id": "db111ab7-8c85-4e20-b004-69f0554db13d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Focus groups", "children": [{"id": "81729b6b-2827-4712-a7c3-8155ccddf41f", "type": "concept", "title": "Recruitment"}, {"id": "19ed4938-6990-4289-bde9-860f4644cc61", "type": "concept", "title": "Moderator guides"}, {"id": "2dad97c3-c8ec-4789-9a12-f26fa24e3e11", "type": "concept", "title": "Group dynamics"}, {"id": "ac537b0e-f19a-415b-b8e1-99956b7cd74c", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality limits"}], "description": "Focus groups help researchers study group meaning-making and community perspectives."}, {"id": "5a5e9dcf-08dd-4490-b81d-e4a8de5cb8a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethnography", "children": [{"id": "ca889737-9bb8-4616-9ecb-fb0c2f537157", "type": "concept", "title": "Participant observation"}, {"id": "43b21575-5acb-40fb-be0a-25555cb9cf18", "type": "concept", "title": "Field notes"}, {"id": "fceb6778-a63d-4d10-90ac-94f64e6f68cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflexivity"}, {"id": "59980559-9918-47cb-896e-6713ff06b300", "type": "concept", "title": "Access and trust"}], "description": "Ethnography helps students study institutional culture and daily practice in context."}]}, {"id": "21d1b1d7-5040-4efa-9d60-49cb14c6bc13", "type": "topic", "title": "Field Observation, Case Studies, and Court or Agency Research", "description": "Study justice organizations in context through observation, case analysis, field notes, and institutional access.", "children": [{"id": "28e6a817-eaef-4f9b-80fa-fb88be4e85e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Observation", "children": [{"id": "2a3fdd57-bf99-45b7-b5fa-73647236d25d", "type": "concept", "title": "Court watching"}, {"id": "3ee7987a-394a-4f60-a8aa-e2b07d55dc92", "type": "concept", "title": "Ride-alongs"}, {"id": "e9c6f6e9-eb73-4956-91bb-2bf8029e08b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency meetings"}, {"id": "866f203a-4e46-4fd4-8fcb-bb73ce50ed1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Systematic observation instruments"}], "description": "Observation teaches students to connect official rules to lived institutional practice."}, {"id": "37fdd093-7d26-47b7-b2f6-2151ac2f39e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case studies", "children": [{"id": "edd5a5c5-d312-4604-9458-da4b7681363a", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-case design"}, {"id": "974b2202-6e10-4d28-b147-603334c164be", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative case study"}, {"id": "e8ecd600-ba9c-46d8-9b99-d3fe42ec033e", "type": "concept", "title": "Process tracing"}, {"id": "75815317-83aa-4c10-a338-f1641361f6a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Document analysis"}], "description": "Case studies provide depth for understanding policy implementation, organizations, and unusual events."}, {"id": "04b1ea72-dde2-4d4f-a867-39e109b5d1a2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutional access", "children": [{"id": "53f6121f-5e4a-4e86-b3e3-3c4fbca565bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Memoranda of understanding"}, {"id": "52103235-70d9-499a-9b35-1aa1e83348e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Gatekeepers"}, {"id": "1eb6a6e8-ca07-4c92-ae08-667ef5f51e24", "type": "concept", "title": "Researcher safety"}, {"id": "b3ac7541-fb65-4758-af51-4fb83d0ca84b", "type": "concept", "title": "Role clarity"}], "description": "Research in justice agencies requires planning, permissions, trust, and boundary management."}]}, {"id": "38bf2abe-008a-4724-b886-e78f6f2e2d53", "type": "topic", "title": "Experiments, Quasi-Experiments, and Program Evaluation", "description": "Evaluate interventions and policies using designs that strengthen causal inference while respecting ethics and feasibility.", "children": [{"id": "7de72e2c-b1f1-41a6-a1d4-ffebc8b82fce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Experiments", "children": [{"id": "7c41fe42-9d46-4479-8447-1ef324ee7fdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Random assignment"}, {"id": "8d867acf-3e68-4a4c-b05e-629065aac91c", "type": "concept", "title": "Treatment and control"}, {"id": "de1e7e2c-614d-4b1b-b780-e66933200f66", "type": "concept", "title": "Field experiments"}, {"id": "6d47b053-fdf1-48c6-bdc5-e565456bdf61", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation fidelity"}], "description": "Experiments can estimate causal effects when random assignment is ethical and feasible."}, {"id": "d015c497-3320-4979-93d6-c0e6e8f1de2e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quasi-experiments", "children": [{"id": "a2f0a040-19dc-463d-be44-ee428b9cff56", "type": "concept", "title": "Difference-in-differences"}, {"id": "867fbd80-ba07-4927-a7a4-be15bddc2112", "type": "concept", "title": "Regression discontinuity"}, {"id": "2e4c6dd4-9c21-41f2-9385-619b2bb0a7b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Matching"}, {"id": "799cd451-c312-451e-997f-c8bd54bdf322", "type": "concept", "title": "Interrupted time series"}], "description": "Quasi-experimental designs strengthen causal claims when randomization is not possible."}, {"id": "4ab1616d-0c3c-490c-9899-32fc4734003f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Program evaluation", "children": [{"id": "11a44abf-2e95-4262-b62a-eb55d9c0c343", "type": "concept", "title": "Logic models"}, {"id": "dfb3d481-8004-4fa7-81c9-a5cc5d4f8a4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Process evaluation"}, {"id": "d51a8f9c-faee-410e-913c-b30ae4d35398", "type": "concept", "title": "Outcome evaluation"}, {"id": "c3c5125c-c19e-4546-8420-f6ab42d1adb9", "type": "concept", "title": "Impact evaluation"}], "description": "Evaluation connects research methods to practical questions about whether programs work."}]}, {"id": "cb20d315-d4a1-4d38-9c7f-9766e88b639f", "type": "topic", "title": "Official Criminal Justice Data and Administrative Records", "description": "Use UCR, NIBRS, NCVS, BJS, court, corrections, and agency records with care and skepticism.", "children": [{"id": "4e134ee2-e19a-42eb-b1b6-d28dd2ca90c4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crime data systems", "children": [{"id": "b53e900f-1465-41f9-ae75-5d90e8e4db8c", "type": "concept", "title": "UCR"}, {"id": "83479786-8c3f-44ca-9f2f-3158906bc248", "type": "concept", "title": "NIBRS"}, {"id": "3acccf70-652e-4c96-b905-33b82d131234", "type": "concept", "title": "FBI Crime Data Explorer"}, {"id": "fd54ff12-8dba-41e0-89b1-8d1ee5bc9b74", "type": "concept", "title": "Clearance data"}], "description": "Official data are powerful but reflect reporting, recording, and enforcement practices."}, {"id": "87151277-71df-480c-b211-9a4e2f744298", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Victimization and justice datasets", "children": [{"id": "e32cf32e-cb99-4e10-96f9-41df22fd2d9a", "type": "concept", "title": "NCVS"}, {"id": "c4f92c87-ad16-4852-9c2e-12da6fe5515f", "type": "concept", "title": "NACJD"}, {"id": "30440a09-0a6e-4a8e-874b-414bbffe1b98", "type": "concept", "title": "BJS Data Analysis Tools"}, {"id": "c7a36028-e060-4239-b9ec-794c81ef4d97", "type": "concept", "title": "Court and corrections datasets"}], "description": "Students learn to find and interpret major public datasets."}, {"id": "a2f98426-4b7f-4fc7-aba1-2611b8b64e95", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Administrative data cautions", "children": [{"id": "830b7ff9-6b99-4a4c-9cac-dad7c725c889", "type": "concept", "title": "Changing definitions"}, {"id": "e7e12b76-5f30-47a4-9a45-4ef4738b5525", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency incentives"}, {"id": "8ae7d336-c585-4687-a188-a51de6dc3789", "type": "concept", "title": "Record linkage"}, {"id": "987ba89e-1cc1-4fb9-8ee4-e3961cb36ea8", "type": "concept", "title": "Data dictionaries"}], "description": "Administrative records are collected for operations, not always for research."}]}, {"id": "f8351417-84a8-48d9-9493-d12f97717fe6", "type": "topic", "title": "Descriptive Statistics and Exploratory Data Analysis", "description": "Summarize justice data clearly before moving to complex inference or policy claims.", "children": [{"id": "dcdb265a-dfe5-473c-82f1-fbb379814b3a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Describing distributions", "children": [{"id": "b517be1c-4249-4d75-a3c6-fe785b0dc343", "type": "concept", "title": "Frequencies"}, {"id": "fe739b22-51cc-426b-8ec4-ebc6b0eebb82", "type": "concept", "title": "Means and medians"}, {"id": "3a1e3b02-70f0-4a8f-822f-e0d62901a6bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Variation"}, {"id": "e62a90f2-f95c-44ec-bc36-c72e3bd20e77", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-tabulations"}], "description": "Exploration helps students understand what the data say before testing claims."}, {"id": "9b5dce6b-bb6c-4df5-98fb-be2312331043", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visualization", "children": [{"id": "7b12e814-855d-4d38-8689-a4f48439fbf0", "type": "concept", "title": "Bar charts"}, {"id": "1c2b7939-433b-472a-8125-229d0df60ad1", "type": "concept", "title": "Line charts"}, {"id": "e3ffe359-64d1-4030-b5e1-48551ceb40e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Maps"}, {"id": "d8e375c3-4861-4b8e-b87a-0c049d32a44b", "type": "concept", "title": "Rates and denominators"}], "description": "Good graphics reveal patterns, comparisons, and uncertainty without misleading the reader."}, {"id": "6f46c8c8-58b3-4a2b-99e3-bb53b1888680", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data cleaning", "children": [{"id": "363f2740-851a-433a-814f-67055c251417", "type": "concept", "title": "Missing values"}, {"id": "174769a0-8a64-495d-bda0-42adaa5749e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Duplicate cases"}, {"id": "3b108aed-c788-439f-b6ee-7283571c280c", "type": "concept", "title": "Recoding"}, {"id": "c03edc0e-ace0-4709-9200-4c97779ab9df", "type": "concept", "title": "Audit trails"}], "description": "Data analysis begins with careful checking and documentation."}]}, {"id": "7e2e8333-6302-4f87-a9ca-1fb3141c5fbe", "type": "topic", "title": "Hypothesis Testing, Association, and Group Comparisons", "description": "Use inferential tools to compare groups, estimate uncertainty, and test empirical claims.", "children": [{"id": "541e3726-65e0-4074-8044-4b0be293b128", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inference foundations", "children": [{"id": "aeea24b4-2f92-4456-8916-a006a34b9af6", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling distributions"}, {"id": "159d40fe-cedc-4452-a8ea-02a8bf4602f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidence intervals"}, {"id": "bb403558-0d6d-4fb9-a810-62f8b9856c7f", "type": "concept", "title": "p-values"}, {"id": "496470db-db94-4964-83be-12a30e581a1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Statistical significance"}], "description": "Inference helps students distinguish patterns in data from random variation."}, {"id": "7bc7426a-80c9-4e50-a9c1-03fa9e2fe12a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Group comparisons", "children": [{"id": "035b3c6b-85a1-43d7-ba9d-e3242b28b2cb", "type": "concept", "title": "t-tests"}, {"id": "d6ff9b60-6255-45ea-8b72-8f92e4837bec", "type": "concept", "title": "ANOVA"}, {"id": "40b576d6-cf1b-47e1-a9df-591900eb2a2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Chi-square"}, {"id": "64c766b6-7ef4-44d9-ae5e-cc6ec6f1b8b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Effect sizes"}], "description": "CJ research often compares outcomes across groups, places, programs, or time periods."}, {"id": "6f8f2ea1-175d-45e8-b319-272174e5a6bb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Association", "children": [{"id": "1ffa54a2-e0df-45ff-a2f0-193e04d7c4ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Correlation"}, {"id": "712e1998-502b-40ac-b842-f98fefb60c21", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-tabs"}, {"id": "bb148c02-ff69-485e-8ec8-e9cb577b11fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk ratios"}, {"id": "ed76ef22-909b-4824-a24e-592a5cdd8e95", "type": "concept", "title": "Odds ratios overview"}], "description": "Association tools show whether variables move together, while reminding students that association is not causation."}]}, {"id": "b9e6b41a-d11b-42b4-b582-95c5e10f975b", "type": "topic", "title": "Regression, Prediction, and Introductory Causal Inference", "description": "Use multivariate models to study relationships, prediction, controls, and causal designs without overclaiming.", "children": [{"id": "1769a285-16d3-4538-bcf2-824cc6358a5f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regression basics", "children": [{"id": "9533465a-0b9d-455c-b7ab-ea5e4686019a", "type": "concept", "title": "Simple regression"}, {"id": "81c6d68e-323b-46c9-90f8-76d4c944020e", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple regression"}, {"id": "8596ef53-4656-4d70-9bef-968a995b9840", "type": "concept", "title": "Logistic regression awareness"}, {"id": "a095c4be-0ce3-4891-89ad-b9e5b1ccb3f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Model assumptions"}], "description": "Regression helps summarize relationships while adjusting for measured covariates."}, {"id": "43e43fbb-67d2-437c-8dc9-cac6c1f48f8e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prediction vs causal inference", "children": [{"id": "798d98d4-0589-4318-a1c7-1a25896f34c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Training and testing"}, {"id": "84a7f8a5-ab20-4822-b669-ca5c8c4c07da", "type": "concept", "title": "Confounding"}, {"id": "ba4c6cd8-4091-4567-b15d-d69edff5cbb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Counterfactuals"}, {"id": "9619180f-e95b-4d82-b8c2-6c635f527ec7", "type": "concept", "title": "External validity"}], "description": "Students learn the difference between predicting outcomes and estimating effects."}, {"id": "cde17373-d485-441e-b1e6-a79498231dc1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible interpretation", "children": [{"id": "c97286fa-c151-485f-9b52-487a3ec421bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Coefficients"}, {"id": "fee97a05-e4ca-4c7b-9f9f-57a53b99d3e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Predicted values"}, {"id": "c61a61c9-5c4f-462f-a694-dd7ffdbcc4a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Robustness checks"}, {"id": "95c56a6c-bfdd-4ac0-9fff-abc4b097ae26", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding causal overclaiming"}], "description": "Models must be interpreted with humility, context, uncertainty, and limitations."}]}, {"id":